WEBVTT
NOTE Cedwyn film, frame 006, en. Timings estimated from the script.

1
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.231
<v the estate surveyor>Dai, pull the chain tight. A hundred links, not one fewer.

2
00:00:12.581 --> 00:00:20.658
<v Dai>There she is, sir. Four chains from the hedge to the stile. But why measure a hill that's always been here?

3
00:00:21.008 --> 00:00:29.085
<v the estate surveyor>Because the estate wants to see on paper what it holds. Cogan, Llandough, Penarth, St Andrews, Sully. Every field, every hedge.

4
00:00:29.435 --> 00:00:35.204
<v Dai>And the river? The Ely and the marsh down there. Are you measuring those too?

5
00:00:35.554 --> 00:00:40.554
<v the estate surveyor>Only the estate's land. Hold the pole straight. The first plan starts today.
